        "parms": "# notein and xnotein — notes from a keyboard\nnotein sends the pitch, velocity and channel of every note that arrives on a MIDI input port, right to left: the channel first, the pitch last. A release reports velocity 0, whether the keyboard sent a note-off or a note-on with velocity 0. xnotein also reports the release velocity: how fast the key came up.\nThe first argument is the input port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. A port that cannot be opened, or no keyboard at all, leaves the object silent, and the patch still loads. On Windows a port can be open in one place at a time, so untick it under Settings › MIDI for a patch to hear it. The second argument is a channel to listen to, 1-16, or 0 for all.\nMax's notein drops its channel outlet when it is given a channel. Here the outlet stays and sends that channel, so the cords keep their places when you add an argument.",
